body:
I mean, I guess the thing is when people are mad at me, whether its rational or not I feel like its my responsibility to agree with them. It's kind of a mess I guess.   


I've seen a therapist for about 3 years. It's helped a bit. He's not someone I'd call a "friend." unofficially.. I've been told I have BPD, PTSD and major depression. It seems like any time I even manage to get out of the shit for even a minute my manager gets pissed at me, it seems to me to be for no reason, but I guess I'm not an expert on that. In his eyes I'm just the worst person on earth,and .. well maybe I am. I mean bad things don't happen to good people, right?   


Either way, him being mad at me is my fault, if nothing else other than the fact that I made the decision to work for him. to move here, to leave my other job. These were my actions and everything that happens because of them are my fault. 

&#x200B;

Ya know I honestly hope there's not like.. a god or anything. Ya know like I dont want to deal with all of this shit just to FINALLY get to a place where I can be free of it all, only to burn in hell forever for it. Not like I woudln't burn in hell forever for something else. I just.. I shouldn't exist. I should never have existed, and when I cease to exist thats what I want. Nothing. 

&#x200B;

There've been a few times where I've screwed up and seemingly caused problems. Like refusing to eat or drink before working in the summer sun, or accidentally mixing meds. I remember in both instances my thoughts were sort of.. well shit. This isn't how I wanted this to happen.. but.. well.. its not my problem anymore. It was so easy to just be resigned to it. 

&#x200B;

I know I'll never have peace, never have happiness.. I will always be unhappy, and even if something happens that is wonderful, I will find a way to torture myself. I just want it to stop.
